course: dictionary
lesson: 14094
title: Memoir: a true story from a life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A memoir is a book or story that someone writes about their own life and memories. It is a noun, and more than one is «memoirs». «I wrote a memoir about the summer we moved house.» The writer is telling a true story about something that really happened to them.
explain: In your writing lessons you write memoir pieces about real events from your own life. You write them in the first person, using «I», so the reader knows the story is true and personal. «I was nervous on my first day at the new school.» The word «I» tells you the story is told in the writer's own voice.
explain: The word can also mean a formal written account, often of someone else's life. «The memoir of the old sailor described the storms he had seen at sea.» Context helps here: the sailor is the one who lived the story. Look for words like «his» or «her» and names of other people to spot a memoir about someone else.
fact: A memoir is a true story that a person writes about their own life and memories.
fact: «Memoir» is a noun. More than one memoir is «memoirs».
fact: «Memoirs» can also mean a book by a famous person about their life and the events they saw.
fact: In your writing lessons, a memoir piece is written in the first person, using «I».
fact: Phrases you may meet: «write a memoir», «a childhood memoir», «publish his memoirs».
exercise: «I wrote a memoir about my first year at school.» What is a memoir? | A poem about the sea | A map of a town | *A true story someone writes about their own life | A list of shopping for the week
exercise: In a memoir piece you write about your own life. Which word shows the writer is telling their own story? | Blue | *I | Under | Yesterday
exercise: «The memoirs of the famous footballer described his life and the big matches he played.» What does memoirs mean here? | A quiet walk in the park | A pair of football boots | *A book by a famous person about their life and the events they saw | A kind of sweet from the shop
test: «My childhood memoir has a chapter about the day we got our dog.» What is a childhood memoir? | *A true story about the writer's own early life | A story about a dragon that flies to the moon | A set of instructions for a game | A science book about dogs
test: What does «publish his memoirs» mean? | Draw pictures for a magazine | Lose his notes in a drawer | Forget everything about his childhood | *Print and share his book about his own life
exam: What tells you that «The memoir of the nurse described the long nights on the ward» is about someone else? | The word ward | The long nights | The word memoir | *It describes the nurse, not «I»
